.Dd November 5, 2026
.Dt DIRNAME 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm dirname
.Nd print the directory component of a path string
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar path
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Print the parent directory of
.Ar path ,
followed by a newline.
Trailing slashes are ignored before finding the last component.
A path without a directory component, including an empty string, produces
a single period;
the root path produces
.Ql / .
The path need not exist: no file is opened.
Quote a path containing spaces and use
.Ql --
before an operand beginning with a dash.
.Sh UNSUPPORTED ON ABSD
This is the unmodified sbase 0.1 utility from the pinned archive, using
Picolibc's path-string operation.
It takes exactly one operand; GNU multiple-operand and NUL-output options
are not provided.
It uses the inherited output stream and acquires no additional authority.
Host reference cases and ABSD ELF checks are distinct from guest execution;
see
.Xr sbase 7 .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success; nonzero for invalid options, missing or extra operands,
or output errors.
Diagnostics use standard error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dirname /home/operator/notes.txt
dirname "two words/notes.txt"
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr basename 1 ,
.Xr filesystem 7 ,
.Xr sbase 7
